[Introduction] Accuracy on the standard benchmarks has risen steadily, from multitask convolutional networks~\cite{daudt2019multitask,yang2022asymmetric} through bi-temporal semantic reasoning and spatio-temporal Transformers~\cite{ding2022bi, ding2024joint} to state-space models~\cite{chen2024changemamba,wijenayake2026mamba}. || [Semantic Change Detection] Bi-SRNet \cite{ding2022bi} and SCanNet~\cite{ding2024joint} added bi-temporal semantic reasoning and spatio-temporal Transformer modelling, and ChangeMask~\cite{zheng2022changemask} decoupled semantic and change branches. || [Student] The task loss is  egin{equation}  egin{split} \mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{task}} ={}& \mathrm{CE}(b,y^{\mathrm{c}}) + \lambda_{\mathrm{sc}}\,\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{sc}} &+ 	frac12 ig[\mathrm{CE}_{
eq0}(s^{1},y^{1})+\mathrm{CE}_{
eq0}(s^{2},y^{2}) ig], \end{split} \end{equation} where $\mathrm{CE}_{
eq0}$ ignores class-0 pixels and $\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{sc}}$ ($\lambda_{\mathrm{sc}}=0.1$) is the bi-temporal feature-consistency loss of Bi-SRNet~\cite{ding2022bi}. || [SECOND] Several papers evaluate on a split of the public training set instead of the official test set~\cite{ding2022bi,ding2024joint}; we use the official split throughout and compare only with results obtained on it.
